---
import SiteLink from '../../../components/SiteLink.astro';
import Layout from '../../../layouts/ProgramLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Art from '../../../components/Art.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import ToolGrid from '../../../components/ToolGrid.astro';
import ProgramEnd from '../../../components/ProgramEnd.astro';
import {fde} from '../../../data/fde';
const base='/programs/forward-deployment-engineer/';
---
<Layout track="fde" section="overview" title="Forward Deployment Engineering" description="A practical AI delivery program for experienced engineers: RAG, agents, multimodal AI, production operations, enterprise integration, and solution architecture.">
<PageHero slot="hero" eyebrow="Program overview" title="Forward Deployment Engineering" description="Turn AI prototypes into solutions teams can use." image="fde-learning" imageAlt="AI-generated learning scene with learners collaborating; not actual academy participants" caption="Discover. Build. Evaluate. Deploy. Improve."><p class="fde-hero-copy">Bring your software experience. Build AI applications, connect enterprise systems, and learn to own the engineering story from customer problem to handover.</p><div class="actions"><SiteLink class="button" href={base+'curriculum/'}>Explore the curriculum <Icon name="arrowRight" /></SiteLink><SiteLink class="text-link" href={base+'projects/'}>See the projects <Icon name="layers" /></SiteLink><SiteLink class="text-link" href="/enquire/?program=fde">Enquire about FDE <Icon name="arrowUpRight" /></SiteLink></div></PageHero>
<section class="container program-facts"><div><Icon name="users" /><strong>Experienced engineers</strong><span>Build on your software foundations</span></div><div><Icon name="book" /><strong>Eight connected modules</strong><span>Readiness through forward deployment</span></div><div><Icon name="layers" /><strong>Three learning projects</strong><span>Knowledge, action, and delivery</span></div><div><Icon name="code" /><strong>Python-led practice</strong><span>Multi-stack integration context</span></div></section>
<section class="container section two-grid editorial"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM BUILDING FEATURES TO DELIVERING SOLUTIONS</p><h2>The code is one part.<br />The context changes everything.</h2><p>A useful AI solution must fit a workflow, respect data boundaries, survive failures, and earn confidence through evidence. This program brings those responsibilities into the learning journey.</p><ul class="check-list"><li>Understand the problem before choosing an AI pattern.</li><li>Connect models, data, tools, and existing systems.</li><li>Measure quality, latency, and cost alongside functionality.</li><li>Explain the design and prepare another engineer to operate it.</li></ul></div><div class="readiness-card"><p class="eyebrow">IS THIS YOUR NEXT STEP?</p><h3>You already build software.</h3><p>You are comfortable with backend development, APIs, JSON, Git, and databases. You may work in Python, .NET, Java, or TypeScript.</p><h3>We connect that experience to AI.</h3><p>Labs use Python as the reference implementation. Architecture and integration discussions connect to other stacks; each lab does not require four separate implementations.</p><SiteLink class="text-link" href={base+'curriculum/#module-1'}>Explore the optional readiness bridge <Icon name="arrowRight" /></SiteLink></div></section>
<section class="tinted section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PROGRESSION</p><h2>One connected delivery journey.</h2></div><p>Move from engineering readiness to an integrated pilot, with evidence and explanation at every stage.</p></div><ol class="fde-journey">{fde.modules.map((m,i)=><li><span class="journey-index">0{i+1}</span><Icon name={m.icon} /><h3>{m.title}</h3><p>{m.summary}</p><SiteLink class="text-link" href={base+`curriculum/#module-${i+1}`}>Explore module <Icon name="arrowRight" /></SiteLink></li>)}</ol></div></section>
<section class="container section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">TOOLS WITH A JOB TO DO</p><h2>A practical engineering toolkit.</h2></div><p>Learn why a tool belongs in the system and where its responsibilities end.</p></div><ToolGrid /><p class="caption">Model providers and tool versions are confirmed before teaching. API credentials stay server-side; recorded responses and simulated tools support repeatable exercises.</p></section>
<section class="tinted section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PROJECTS</p><h2>Build evidence of your decisions.</h2></div><SiteLink class="text-link" href={base+'projects/'}>Inside the projects <Icon name="arrowRight" /></SiteLink></div><div class="three-grid">{fde.projects.map(p=><article class="fde-project-preview"><Art name={p.image} alt={`Concept illustration for ${p.title}`} /><div><p class="eyebrow">{p.tag}</p><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.summary}</p><SiteLink class="text-link" href={base+'projects/#'+p.id}>Explore the project <Icon name="arrowUpRight" /></SiteLink></div></article>)}</div><p class="caption">Planned learning projects using illustrative scenarios and sample data, not client assignments or past student results.</p></div></section>
<section class="container section two-grid editorial"><Art name="career-path" alt="Illustration of the progression from engineering practice to presenting a portfolio" /><div><p class="eyebrow">EXPLAIN THE WORK. OWN THE STORY.</p><h2>Prepare for the technical conversation.</h2><p>Practise architecture interviews, customer discovery, incident debugging, and stakeholder demonstrations. Build a delivery case study that connects the problem, the decisions, and the results.</p><SiteLink class="button" href={base+'career-preparation/'}>Explore career preparation <Icon name="message" /></SiteLink></div></section>
<section class="container section faq-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">PROGRAM ARRANGEMENTS</p><h2>Plan your next step.</h2>{[['When does it start?','Dates, duration, weekly commitment, fees, and delivery arrangements will be announced when confirmed.'],['Do I need to be a Python developer?','You should be comfortable building software. Python is the reference lab language; the readiness bridge and integration discussions support engineers from .NET, Java, and TypeScript backgrounds. Final entry requirements will be confirmed before enrolment.'],['Will I work on client systems?','The published projects are learning scenarios using sample data and simulated enterprise services. They do not require access to employer systems or confidential documents.'],['What will I leave with?','The learning opportunities include repositories, architecture diagrams, evaluation reports, demonstrations, and a delivery case study. Employment, certification, or production-readiness outcomes are not promised.']].map(([q,a])=><details class="faq"><summary>{q}<Icon name="plus" /></summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}</section><ProgramEnd track="fde" />
</Layout>
